1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:03,340
In this town, every Friday, the world flips upside down.

2
00:00:04,427 --> 00:00:07,404
At exactly three o'clock, gravity goes the other way.

3
00:00:08,393 --> 00:00:10,765
Everyone grabs the handles on the ceiling.

4
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:13,628
Houses have doors on the roof.

5
00:00:14,293 --> 00:00:15,755
Trees grow both ways.

6
00:00:16,227 --> 00:00:18,295
Pizza is always eaten upside down.

7
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:21,634
For one hour, the sky is the floor.

8
00:00:22,527 --> 00:00:24,595
Then at four, everything flips back.

9
00:00:25,260 --> 00:00:25,813
Easy.

10
00:00:27,060 --> 00:00:29,431
My little brother Milo loves Flip Friday.

11
00:00:30,227 --> 00:00:33,507
He keeps his shoes on the ceiling just for fun.

12
00:00:34,593 --> 00:00:36,662
But this Friday, something was wrong.

13
00:00:37,327 --> 00:00:39,395
At three o'clock, the world flipped.

14
00:00:40,060 --> 00:00:42,431
At four o'clock... it didn't flip back.

15
00:00:43,227 --> 00:00:44,083
Five o'clock.

16
00:00:45,027 --> 00:00:45,883
Six o'clock.

17
00:00:46,827 --> 00:00:47,380
Midnight.

18
00:00:48,627 --> 00:00:50,695
People started living on the ceiling.

19
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:52,822
Sleeping on the ceiling.

20
00:00:53,293 --> 00:00:54,755
Cooking on the ceiling.

21
00:00:55,227 --> 00:00:56,386
Milo was thrilled.

22
00:00:57,027 --> 00:00:58,186
I was not.

23
00:00:58,827 --> 00:01:00,319
Because I noticed something.

24
00:01:00,760 --> 00:01:04,040
Every hour, the sky below us got a little closer.

25
00:01:05,127 --> 00:01:06,892
The clouds were reaching up.

26
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,013
Grabbing.

27
00:01:09,260 --> 00:01:09,813
Pulling.

28
00:01:11,060 --> 00:01:12,522
The town was falling.

29
00:01:12,993 --> 00:01:14,152
Into the sky.

30
00:01:14,793 --> 00:01:17,771
I found the flip switch inside the old windmill.

31
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:19,919
It was stuck.

32
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:22,931
Someone had jammed it with a shoe.

33
00:01:23,727 --> 00:01:24,886
A tiny shoe.

34
00:01:25,527 --> 00:01:26,383
Milo's shoe.

35
00:01:27,327 --> 00:01:30,304
"I just wanted it to last longer," he said.

36
00:01:31,293 --> 00:01:33,058
I pulled the shoe out.

37
00:01:33,627 --> 00:01:35,089
The world flipped back.

38
00:01:35,560 --> 00:01:37,022
Everyone hit the ground.

39
00:01:37,493 --> 00:01:40,168
Every Friday since, Milo keeps both shoes on.

40
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:44,340
And the sky still looks at us... like it's hungry.

